# NIZAM - environment template for the `life-agent` service. TEMPLATE ONLY. NOTHING HERE IS EXECUTED.
#
# Owning contract: PFOS 12 - Two-Agent VPS Deployment & Operations, §3.1 (six things are separate,
#   the environment file among them), §3.2.7 (root-owned, mode-restricted, one per service, read by
#   no other service), §5.2/§5.3 (the two authenticity checks and the allowlist), §5.5.5 (bounded
#   concurrency), §6.2 (per-agent cap isolation), §6.3 (the eligibility registry), §8 (the kill
#   switch, in both forms), §7.6 (this path).
# Spec: .kiro/specs/06-two-agent-vps/ - task 7.3. Contract 12, phase 7. Requirements R6, R11, R12,
#   R15, R17, R18, R23, R24.
# Steering: .kiro/steering/two-agent-vps.md §0b (no deployment particular in a tracked file),
#   §1 (the life agent is Python and lives in the OTHER repository), §2 (writing this file is
#   permitted, running it is not), §4 invariant 6 (both agents honour the coarse halt and their own
#   weekly cap), §7 (placeholders only, AC09).
#
# Companions: ops/docker-compose.yml declares this file as this service's single env_file, under the
#   placeholder <LIFE_ENV_PATH>. Audited by src/server/ops/envTemplates.ts, which every test run
#   re-checks, including the check that no entry here appears in the finance file unless it is a
#   declared shared entry that is not a secret.
#
# WHY THIS FILE LIVES IN THIS REPOSITORY AT ALL. The life agent's code is in the other repository
# and Kiro must not touch it (steering §6). Its environment file is here because the boundary
# shapes - the bus envelope, the recovery band, the transport guards, the cap - are agreed in one
# place, and this repository is that place. The entry names below are bound to the port
# configuration interfaces under src/server/ports/, so a rename there surfaces as a finding rather
# than as a template that quietly stops matching the agreement.
#
# HOW TO READ AN ENTRY. Each assignment is preceded by exactly three annotation lines:
#   what:    one line saying what the value is
#   gate:    which human gate in ops/DEPLOYMENT_CONTROL.md supplies it - G1..G8, or `operator` for a
#            value the operator simply chooses, or `build` for a path to an artefact the build emits
#   secret:  yes if disclosing the value would let someone reach or impersonate this deployment
#
# EVERY VALUE IS AN <ANGLE_BRACKET> PLACEHOLDER WHOSE NAME IS ITS OWN ENTRY NAME. No example value,
# no redacted stand-in of the right length, and no comment showing a value's shape or width.
#
# THIS FILE CONTAINS NO FINANCE SECRET. Not the finance bot token, not the finance model key, not
# the finance webhook secret. That is the whole point of gate G4 minting two keys instead of one
# (contract 12 T4): a runaway loop in this agent cannot spend the other agent's allocation, and a
# compromise of this file does not yield the other agent.

# ---- the store (contract 06 §2.1: this agent's own directory, and no fallback) ----------------

# what: the absolute directory this agent's store lives in; its own volume, mounted nowhere else
# gate: G1
# secret: no
LIFE_DATA_DIR=<LIFE_DATA_DIR>

# what: the store file name within that directory
# gate: operator
# secret: no
LIFE_STORE_FILE=<LIFE_STORE_FILE>

# what: how long a writer waits on a lock before a busy failure surfaces to its caller
# gate: operator
# secret: no
STORE_BUSY_TIMEOUT_MS=<STORE_BUSY_TIMEOUT_MS>

# ---- the transport (contract 12 §5) ----------------------------------------------------------

# what: the port this agent listens on inside its own network; no agent binds a public port
# gate: operator
# secret: no
LIFE_CONTAINER_PORT=<LIFE_CONTAINER_PORT>

# what: this agent's bot token
# gate: G3
# secret: yes
BOT_A_TOKEN=<BOT_A_TOKEN>

# what: the secret token the provider echoes on every delivery to this agent; absent fails closed
# gate: G6
# secret: yes
LIFE_WEBHOOK_SECRET=<LIFE_WEBHOOK_SECRET>

# what: the operator identifiers permitted to interact; an empty list means nobody, not everybody
# gate: G3
# secret: no
ALLOWED_USER_IDS=<ALLOWED_USER_IDS>

# what: the messaging provider's documented bot API base, resolved from its own documentation
# gate: operator
# secret: no
MSG_API_BASE=<MSG_API_BASE>

# what: webhook or the documented long-poll fallback; a mode, with the same guards either way
# gate: operator
# secret: no
TELEGRAM_MODE=<TELEGRAM_MODE>

# what: bounded worker concurrency, because a single-operator system needs very little
# gate: operator
# secret: no
MAX_WORK_ITEMS=<MAX_WORK_ITEMS>

# ---- model routing (contract 12 §6, and contracts 09/10/11 for the roster) --------------------

# what: this agent's own model key, with its own provider-side periodic limit
# gate: G4
# secret: yes
OR_KEY_LIFE=<OR_KEY_LIFE>

# what: the model provider's documented API base, resolved from its own documentation
# gate: operator
# secret: no
MODEL_API_BASE=<MODEL_API_BASE>

# what: this agent's weekly spend ceiling, in the provider's own accounting unit
# gate: G4
# secret: no
LIFE_WEEKLY_CAP=<LIFE_WEEKLY_CAP>

# what: where the eligibility registry is read from; a provisional one refuses routing
# gate: build
# secret: no
MODEL_ELIGIBILITY_REGISTRY_PATH=<MODEL_ELIGIBILITY_REGISTRY_PATH>

# ---- the consent channel (contract 12 §4, R9) -------------------------------------------------

# what: where the bus listens on the internal network; unreachable from outside it by construction
# gate: operator
# secret: no
BUS_INTERNAL_ENDPOINT=<BUS_INTERNAL_ENDPOINT>

# ---- recovery context (contract 12 §4.3: a band crosses, a figure never does) -----------------

# what: the recovery provider's documented API base, resolved from its own documentation
# gate: operator
# secret: no
WHOOP_API_BASE=<WHOOP_API_BASE>

# what: the recovery provider credential; held by this agent only, and never by the finance agent
# gate: operator
# secret: yes
WHOOP_ACCESS_TOKEN=<WHOOP_ACCESS_TOKEN>

# ---- the kill switch, both forms (contract 12 §8, steering §4 invariant 6) --------------------

# what: the sentinel path checked before every model call, model-path write, and bus publish
# gate: G1
# secret: no
KILL_SENTINEL_PATH=<KILL_SENTINEL_PATH>

# what: the coarse halt; 1 halts this agent, 0 does not. Restart-scoped, so it is not a panic stop
# gate: operator
# secret: no
NIZAM_KILL_ALL=<NIZAM_KILL_ALL>

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# What is deliberately absent
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# 1. NO WEBHOOK PATH SEGMENT. The path routes at the proxy (contract 12 §2.2.3) and this agent
#    never needs its own. Holding it here would put it in a second place for no benefit, and
#    §2.2.4's reason for keeping that class of value out of proxy logs applies to files too.
#
# 2. NO FINANCE ENTRY OF ANY KIND. No finance token, key, cap, store path, or container port.
#    Gate G4's own verification line is the negative one: the life file must contain no finance key.
#
# 3. NO STORE PATH BELONGING TO ANOTHER AGENT. Neither agent's volume is mounted into the other's
#    container, so even a guessed path would not resolve (§3.2.1). There is nothing to name.
#
# 4. NO CROSS-STORE OPEN OF ANY KIND, and therefore no entry that could configure one. The other
#    agent's store is not present in this namespace (§3.2.1) and the statement that would join two
#    stores is refused by the code as well (contract 06 §2.1.3).
#
# 5. NO DEFAULT FOR ANYTHING. An unset entry is a startup failure, not a guess: there is no default
#    endpoint, no default cap, and no default allowlist. An unconfigured guard must not be an open
#    door (§5.2, §5.3).
